Previously the handler implemented `evaluate` and safely returned an empty result. Either keep a concrete stub implementing the abstract methods, or keep the old `DetectorHandler` subclass until the real implementation exists."}, {"file": "src/sentry/workflow_engine/processors/detector.py", "line": 230, "severity": "low", "title": "Docstring still says evaluate returns a list", "body": "The `StatefulDetectorHandler.evaluate` docstring still says it "returns a list of `DetectorEvaluationResult`". After this change it returns a dict keyed by `DetectorGroupKey`, so the docstring misleads implementers and callers about the return type."}]}
